<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 1.49 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 1.49 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.2410 to the dollar, up from 3.2430 on Thursday and at 1.8760 to the mark, down from 1.8745, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.49 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Thursday's 1.51 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
